{:edb/db-before-t 1373 :edb/db-after-t 1374 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534686 50 #inst "2026-10-08T04:10:17.435Z" 13194139534686 true] [17592186059772 1020 #edb/ref 17592186303335 13194139534686 true] [17592186059772 1020 #edb/ref 17592186303339 13194139534686 true] [17592186059772 1020 #edb/ref 17592186303343 13194139534686 true] [17592186059773 1020 #edb/ref 17592186303307 13194139534686 true] [17592186059773 1020 #edb/ref 17592186303350 13194139534686 true] [17592186059773 1020 #edb/ref 17592186303357 13194139534686 true] [17592186059774 1020 #edb/ref 17592186303314 13194139534686 true] [17592186059774 1020 #edb/ref 17592186303321 13194139534686 true] [17592186059774 1020 #edb/ref 17592186303328 13194139534686 true] [17592186059774 1020 #edb/ref 17592186303364 13194139534686 true] [17592186277617 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303338 13194139534686 true] [17592186303307 1017 #edb/ref 17592186303308 13194139534686 true] [17592186303307 1089 "q-128476" 13194139534686 true] [17592186303307 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534686 true] [17592186303307 1100 "Which of the following statements are true regarding the matrix $T$ given below?\n\n- $T$ is a singular matrix\n- $T$ is **not** a singular matrix\n- $det(T)=-30$\n\n \n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & -5 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$" 13194139534686 true] [17592186303307 1113 #uuid "1de7b7b6-d74a-53dc-9249-a5265a42e232" 13194139534686 true] [17592186303307 1145 "Remember that a square matrix is singular if its determinant is equal to $0.$\n\nUsing the formula, we take the alternating sum of the entries in the top row of the matrix, multiplied by their respective minors, as follows:  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(T) & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & -5 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}|-3|\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}|-5|\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1(1-3)-3(2-1)-5(6-1) \\\\  & =1\\cdot (-2)-3\\cdot 1-5\\cdot 5 \\\\  & =-2-3-25 \\\\  & =-30\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSince $det(T)=-30\\ne 0$, the matrix is **not** singular. \n\nTherefore, only statements II and III are true." 13194139534686 true] [17592186303308 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303309 13194139534686 true] [17592186303308 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303310 13194139534686 true] [17592186303308 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303311 13194139534686 true] [17592186303308 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303312 13194139534686 true] [17592186303308 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303313 13194139534686 true] [17592186303308 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534686 true] [17592186303308 1041 "selection" 13194139534686 true] [17592186303308 1104 #edb/ref 17592186303309 13194139534686 true] [17592186303308 1110 #uuid "9d5536c7-7d93-5b6f-bcb0-08074eb5662e" 13194139534686 true] [17592186303309 1034 "II and III only" 13194139534686 true] [17592186303309 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534686 true] [17592186303309 1111 #uuid "8a191dba-16dd-5b91-b92c-74456c9286df" 13194139534686 true] [17592186303310 1034 "I and III only" 13194139534686 true] [17592186303310 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534686 true] [17592186303310 1111 #uuid "b5b00579-93ef-5741-b329-98cc98e20e8c" 13194139534686 true] [17592186303311 1034 "I only" 13194139534686 true] [17592186303311 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534686 true] [17592186303311 1111 #uuid "e0e1a3d4-3256-56a2-8579-d0cb7725057f" 13194139534686 true] [17592186303312 1034 "III only" 13194139534686 true] [17592186303312 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534686 true] [17592186303312 1111 #uuid "d91db950-9a7f-5572-9414-c66c3ae0f4a5" 13194139534686 true] [17592186303313 1034 "II only" 13194139534686 true] [17592186303313 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534686 true] [17592186303313 1111 #uuid "8dac9c91-67ef-5130-939b-a0b625916607" 13194139534686 true] [17592186303314 1017 #edb/ref 17592186303315 13194139534686 true] [17592186303314 1089 "q-18252" 13194139534686 true] [17592186303314 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534686 true] [17592186303314 1100 "Find the possible values of the constant $p$ given that the matrix $[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 6 & -5 & 2p-4\\end{aligned}]$ is singular." 13194139534686 true] [17592186303314 1113 #uuid "799ed291-cfbc-56bf-891a-7ba1b277d3e5" 13194139534686 true] [17592186303314 1145 "First, let's use our formula to find an expression for the determinant in terms of $p:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 6 & -5 & 2p-4\\end{aligned}| & =1|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ -5 & 2p-4\\end{aligned}|-0|\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ 6 & 2p-4\\end{aligned}|+1|\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 6 & -5\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(2p-4+10)-0+(-10-6) \\\\  & =2p-4+10-10-6 \\\\  & =2p-10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the matrix is singular, the determinant is $0.$ So,  we have:\n\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2p-10 & =0 \\\\ 2p & =10 \\\\ p & =\\frac{10}{2} \\\\  & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $p=5.$" 13194139534686 true] [17592186303315 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303316 13194139534686 true] [17592186303315 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303317 13194139534686 true] [17592186303315 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303318 13194139534686 true] [17592186303315 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303319 13194139534686 true] [17592186303315 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303320 13194139534686 true] [17592186303315 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534686 true] [17592186303315 1041 "selection" 13194139534686 true] [17592186303315 1104 #edb/ref 17592186303320 13194139534686 true] [17592186303315 1110 #uuid "abfe5887-0d05-5018-9ee0-2ab1a972fca7" 13194139534686 true] [17592186303316 1034 "-5" 13194139534686 true] [17592186303316 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534686 true] [17592186303316 1111 #uuid "c19ee59f-4480-595d-be78-0612dc30906d" 13194139534686 true] [17592186303317 1034 "3" 13194139534686 true] [17592186303317 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534686 true] [17592186303317 1111 #uuid "e68058e1-4682-5ab8-b703-62cc2f118682" 13194139534686 true] [17592186303318 1034 "2" 13194139534686 true] [17592186303318 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534686 true] [17592186303318 1111 #uuid "8e5485a5-a0ae-50cc-8dbe-9aab77f55a9b" 13194139534686 true] [17592186303319 1034 "-3" 13194139534686 true] [17592186303319 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534686 true] [17592186303319 1111 #uuid "d6bee06f-bbf2-5d38-83f4-80d000dc236e" 13194139534686 true] [17592186303320 1034 "5" 13194139534686 true] [17592186303320 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534686 true] [17592186303320 1111 #uuid "45831162-173d-54b1-b3e2-550e320a21bf" 13194139534686 true] [17592186303321 1017 #edb/ref 17592186303322 13194139534686 true] [17592186303321 1089 "q-18256" 13194139534686 true] [17592186303321 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534686 true] [17592186303321 1100 "Given that the determinant of \n$[\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 & 3 \\\\ -3y & -2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & y & -5\\end{aligned}]$\n is $81,$ find all the possible values of $y.$" 13194139534686 true] [17592186303321 1113 #uuid "01aa8d57-113b-5436-b1ef-e962e4723b9f" 13194139534686 true] [17592186303321 1145 "Let's use our formula to find an expression for the determinant in terms of $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 & 3 \\\\ -3y & -2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & y & -5\\end{aligned}| & =4|\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ y & -5\\end{aligned}|-2|\\begin{aligned}-3y & 1 \\\\ 2 & -5\\end{aligned}|+3|\\begin{aligned}-3y & -2 \\\\ 2 & y\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =4\\cdot (10-y)-2\\cdot (15y-2)+3\\cdot (-3{y}^{2}+4) \\\\  & =40-4y-30y+4-9{y}^{2}+12 \\\\  & =-9{y}^{2}-34y+56\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the determinant of the matrix is $81,$ we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-9{y}^{2}-34y+56 & =81 \\\\ -9{y}^{2}-34y-25 & =0 \\\\ 9{y}^{2}+34y+25 & =0 \\\\ y & =\\frac{-34\\pm \\sqrt{{34}^{2}-4\\cdot 9\\cdot 25}}{2\\cdot 9} \\\\  & =\\frac{-34\\pm \\sqrt{256}}{18} \\\\  & =\\frac{-34\\pm 16}{18} \\\\  & =\\frac{-17\\pm 8}{9}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $y=-\\frac{25}{9}$ and $y=-1.$" 13194139534686 true] [17592186303322 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303323 13194139534686 true] [17592186303322 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303324 13194139534686 true] [17592186303322 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303325 13194139534686 true] [17592186303322 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303326 13194139534686 true] [17592186303322 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303327 13194139534686 true] [17592186303322 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534686 true] [17592186303322 1041 "selection" 13194139534686 true] [17592186303322 1104 #edb/ref 17592186303327 13194139534686 true] [17592186303322 1110 #uuid "59e39d2d-4575-5e43-a400-caa5668def86" 13194139534686 true] [17592186303323 1034 "$-\\frac{25}{9}$ and $1$ only" 13194139534686 true] [17592186303323 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534686 true] [17592186303323 1111 #uuid "20471aec-848e-513e-968a-d6aec97caa96" 13194139534686 true] [17592186303324 1034 "$-\\frac{5}{3}$ and $1$ only" 13194139534686 true] [17592186303324 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534686 true] [17592186303324 1111 #uuid "b476adf8-40ae-54da-ac98-df291a8dd1ff" 13194139534686 true] [17592186303325 1034 "$-1$ only" 13194139534686 true] [17592186303325 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534686 true] [17592186303325 1111 #uuid "09c5767d-a3b0-5d1a-860a-026fafd6510c" 13194139534686 true] [17592186303326 1034 "$-\\frac{5}{3}$ and $-1$ only" 13194139534686 true] [17592186303326 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534686 true] [17592186303326 1111 #uuid "f5001a26-00b9-5b68-b868-a2749147bd0f" 13194139534686 true] [17592186303327 1034 "$-\\frac{25}{9}$ and $-1$ only" 13194139534686 true] [17592186303327 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534686 true] [17592186303327 1111 #uuid "e19af8f1-f3a5-5db5-ac86-072cb48385c8" 13194139534686 true] [17592186303328 1017 #edb/ref 17592186303329 13194139534686 true] [17592186303328 1089 "q-18272" 13194139534686 true] [17592186303328 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534686 true] [17592186303328 1100 "Given that $M=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 1 & p & 0 \\\\ p-3 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]$ and $det(M)=-23,$ find all the possible values of $p.$" 13194139534686 true] [17592186303328 1113 #uuid "408197de-567d-5d88-85f3-7d29be5c6d83" 13194139534686 true] [17592186303328 1145 "Let's use our formula to find an expression for the determinant in terms of $p:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}(M) & =|\\begin{aligned}0 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 1 & p & 0 \\\\ p-3 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =0|\\begin{aligned}p & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}|-(-3)|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ p-3 & -1\\end{aligned}|+2|\\begin{aligned}1 & p \\\\ p-3 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =0+3\\cdot (-1)+2\\cdot (3p-{p}^{2}) \\\\  & =-3-2{p}^{2}+6p \\\\  & =-2{p}^{2}+6p-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the determinant of the matrix is $-23,$ we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2{p}^{2}+6p-3 & =-23 \\\\ 2{p}^{2}-6p-20 & =0 \\\\ {p}^{2}-3p-10 & =0 \\\\ p & =\\frac{-(-3)\\pm \\sqrt{(-3)^{2}-4\\cdot 1\\cdot (-10)}}{2\\cdot 1} \\\\  & =\\frac{3\\pm \\sqrt{49}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{3\\pm 7}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,  the solutions are $p=-2$ and $p=5.$" 13194139534686 true] [17592186303329 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303330 13194139534686 true] [17592186303329 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303331 13194139534686 true] [17592186303329 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303332 13194139534686 true] [17592186303329 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303333 13194139534686 true] [17592186303329 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303334 13194139534686 true] [17592186303329 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534686 true] [17592186303329 1041 "selection" 13194139534686 true] [17592186303329 1104 #edb/ref 17592186303332 13194139534686 true] [17592186303329 1110 #uuid "47ef13ae-3048-55d4-a544-a1da4c5bbca1" 13194139534686 true] [17592186303330 1034 "$4$ only" 13194139534686 true] [17592186303330 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534686 true] [17592186303330 1111 #uuid "b3d28b60-d649-5c6d-8573-0304c956c863" 13194139534686 true] [17592186303331 1034 "$2$ and $4$ only" 13194139534686 true] [17592186303331 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194