 \\\\  & =(-3+4)-2\\cdot (-\\sqrt{3}) \\\\  & =1+2\\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $det(S)=1+2\\sqrt{3}\\ne 0$, the matrix is **not ** singular. \n\nTherefore, only statement I is true." 13194139534686 true] [17592186303351 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303352 13194139534686 true] [17592186303351 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303353 13194139534686 true] [17592186303351 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303354 13194139534686 true] [17592186303351 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303355 13194139534686 true] [17592186303351 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303356 13194139534686 true] [17592186303351 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534686 true] [17592186303351 1041 "selection" 13194139534686 true] [17592186303351 1104 #edb/ref 17592186303352 13194139534686 true] [17592186303351 1110 #uuid "e5ffcb6e-0917-5f6f-a0aa-f5850879ca37" 13194139534686 true] [17592186303352 1034 "I  only" 13194139534686 true] [17592186303352 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534686 true] [17592186303352 1111 #uuid "9def4b4a-1dd6-546f-a05a-5cec780136ac" 13194139534686 true] [17592186303353 1034 "II and III only" 13194139534686 true] [17592186303353 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534686 true] [17592186303353 1111 #uuid "ea8d1bfd-dd9d-5df0-bb07-aecfb19ecda9" 13194139534686 true] [17592186303354 1034 "I and III  only" 13194139534686 true] [17592186303354 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534686 true] [17592186303354 1111 #uuid "e3c5ada5-b582-58a4-9b16-63c359d07add" 13194139534686 true] [17592186303355 1034 "III only" 13194139534686 true] [17592186303355 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534686 true] [17592186303355 1111 #uuid "19695a11-6184-50a6-b7e4-a8ce98068372" 13194139534686 true] [17592186303356 1034 "II only" 13194139534686 true] [17592186303356 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534686 true] [17592186303356 1111 #uuid "7e56084e-c049-5d03-8053-7d8f8a131ad4" 13194139534686 true] [17592186303357 1017 #edb/ref 17592186303358 13194139534686 true] [17592186303357 1089 "q-77478" 13194139534686 true] [17592186303357 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534686 true] [17592186303357 1100 "Which of the following statements are true regarding the matrix $R$ given below?\n\n- $R$ is a singular matrix\n- $det(R)=0$\n- $det(R)=1$\n\n \n\n$$\nR=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{5} & \\frac{2}{5} & \\frac{1}{5} \\\\ 1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{2} & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$" 13194139534686 true] [17592186303357 1113 #uuid "24cc52a8-4124-5277-acdf-def6004941a2" 13194139534686 true] [17592186303357 1145 "Remember that a square matrix is singular if its determinant is equal to $0.$\n\nUsing the formula, we take the alternating sum of the entries in the top row of the matrix, multiplied by their respective minors, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(R) & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{5} & \\frac{2}{5} & \\frac{1}{5} \\\\ 1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{2} & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{5}|\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2} & 1\\end{aligned}|-\\frac{2}{5}|\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|+\\frac{1}{5}|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{5}(2-\\frac{3}{2})-\\frac{2}{5}(1-0)+\\frac{1}{5}(\\frac{1}{2}-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{5}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{2}{5}\\cdot 1+\\frac{1}{5}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{10}-\\frac{2}{5}+\\frac{1}{10} \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSince $det(R)=0$, the matrix is singular. \n\nTherefore, only statements I and II are true." 13194139534686 true] [17592186303358 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303359 13194139534686 true] [17592186303358 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303360 13194139534686 true] [17592186303358 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303361 13194139534686 true] [17592186303358 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303362 13194139534686 true] [17592186303358 1000 #edb/ref 17592186303363 13194139534686 true] [17592186303358 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534686 true] [17592186303358 1041 "selection" 13194139534686 true] [17592186303358 1104 #edb/ref 17592186303363 13194139534686 true] [17592186303358 1110 #uuid "92720cbe-efa5-5123-a597-8ee071c3b10d" 13194139534686 true] [17592186303359 1034 "II and III only" 13194139534686 true] [17592186303359 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534686 true] [17592186303359 1111 #uuid "b9405d7f-2eab-599d-9ba5-e87cacabdf95" 13194139534686 true] [17592186303360 1034 "I and III only" 13194139534686 true] [17592186303360 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534686 true] [17592186303360 1111 #uuid "8b70e71f-f769-57db-b7fb-a5767752d8e1" 13194139534686 true] [17592186303361 1034 "I only" 13194139534686 true] [17592186303361 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534686 true] [17592186303361 1111 #uuid "916c7451-7165-5939-b18f-f24a87f57db6" 13194139534686 true] [17592186303362 1034 "III only" 13194139534686 true] [17592186303362 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534686 true] [17592186303362 1111 #uuid "8e92102a-d2be-58f6-bc96-f9d23e118a46" 13194139534686 true] [17592186303363 1034 "I and II only" 13194139534686 true] [17592186303363 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534686 true] [17592186303363 1111 #uuid "341dcfd3-2a7a-54a5-a51a-2cd79256e8e3" 13194139534686 true] [17592186303364 1017 #edb/ref 17592186303365 13194139534686 true] [17592186303364 1089 "q-9911" 13194139534686 true] [17592186303364 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534686 true] [17592186303364 1100 "Find the possible values of the constant $k$ given that the matrix\n$[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & k \\\\ 1 & k & -k \\\\ 5 & k & k\\end{aligned}]$ is singular." 13194139534686 true] [17592186303364 1113 #uuid "b27fea7a-77af-5ede-b5e2-28d0928e1d9b" 13194139534686 true] [17592186303364 1145 "First, let's use our formula to find an expression for the determinant in terms of $k:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & k \\\\ 1 & k & -k \\\\ 5 & k & k\\end{aligned}| & =1|\\begin{aligned}k & -k \\\\ k & k\\end{aligned}|-(-1)|\\begin{aligned}1 & -k \\\\ 5 & k\\end{aligned}|+k|\\begin{aligned}1 & k \\\\ 5 & k\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =({k}^{2}+{k}^{2})+(k+5k)+k(k-5k) \\\\  & =2{k}^{2}+6k+k\\cdot (-4k) \\\\